# Web Hosting and Storage Boundary for NaProjectPortal
- This rule defines the hard boundary between static application source code and dynamic, user-action-driven project data. 
- The Core App source code is hosted as a static site (GitHub Pages). Cloudflare R2 is used only for dynamic project content that must be read and written at runtime.

## Hard Constraints
- We must not store, write, or persist dynamic project content in the GitHub Pages repository, its deployed output, or any static hosting location. 
- GitHub Pages is read-only at runtime and cannot be written to and exists to serve the static source code for the Core App.
- Do not invent alternative storage locations for dynamic content. 
- Always Use Cloudflare R2 for persistence unless a different persistence service is explicitly specified in the task requirements.

## Cloudflare Structure and Path Mirroring
- R2 object key prefixes must mirror the local directory structure for predictable uploads, predictable URLs, and simple automation scripts. 
- When adding new dynamic content locations, the same relative folder structure must exist locally and in the bucket key prefix.
- Not all local content is automatically uploaded. 
- Only upload files that are required by the relevant app modules and serverless functions. 
- If unsure, default to not uploading and add an explicit note in the change describing what module/function requires the file and why.

# CDN - Cloudflare R2 Bucket - Domain Name & URL Structure

## CDN Domain and URL Shape
The CDN base domain is: `https://cdn.noble-architecture.com/`

### An R2 object at key:
`NaProjectPortal/26-Projects/AA00__ExampleProjectStructure/10__ProjectAdmin__AppContent/ProjectAdminContent__FilesHere__.txt`

### is served at:
`https://cdn.noble-architecture.com/NaProjectPortal/26-Projects/AA00__ExampleProjectStructure/10__ProjectAdmin__AppContent/ProjectAdminContent__FilesHere__.txt`

## Local-to-CDN Mapping Expectation

#### Local path example:
`D:\WE10_--_Public-Repo_--_Live-Website\na-project-portal\26-Projects\AA00__ExampleProjectStructure\10__ProjectAdmin__AppContent\ProjectAdminContent__FilesHere__.txt`

maps to R2 key (relative from the project root’s published content base):
`NaProjectPortal/26-Projects/AA00__ExampleProjectStructure/10__ProjectAdmin__AppContent/ProjectAdminContent__FilesHere__.txt`

Bucket and Root Prefix

R2 bucket name:
`noble-architecture-cdn`

All NaProjectPortal content in R2 must live under this prefix:
`NaProjectPortal/`

Project grouping convention under NaProjectPortal is:
`NaProjectPortal/<YY>-Projects/<ProjectCode__Name>/`   //<-- YY = Year of the project, projects are grouped in a directory by year.


## Treat the following as dynamic and store in R2:
- user-editable project content
- Authentication/session-related artifacts if persisted
- Document signing artifacts and audit outputs
- Auto-generated emails or their persisted payloads
- Any other user-persistent data or user-action logs.


## Definitions
*Static source code*
- Static source code means the repository code that builds and deploys the Core App. 
- Static source code belongs in the GitHub Pages repo and must not depend on writing to GitHub Pages at runtime.

*Dynamic project content*
- Dynamic project content means any data created, modified, or persisted as a result of a user action or serverless function execution. 
- Dynamic project content must be stored in the Cloudflare R2 bucket and accessed via the Cloudflare APIs. 
- If a user action is involved, treat the output as dynamic unless explicitly stated otherwise.